TASK SPECIFICATIONS:
{
  "id": "PUB011",
  "title": "Automated Production Line Control",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "requirements": "# Automated Production Line Control\n\n- **Difficulty:** Medium (medium)\n\n## Requirements\n\nA simple automated production line consists of three workstations: Workstation A, Workstation B, and Workstation C. The product needs to go through these three stations in sequence to be considered fully completed. There is a motor in the production line that is responsible for moving the product from one workstation to the next. The sequence of the line is from Workstation A to Workstation B, and then to Workstation C. Each workstation has a sensor (used to detect if the product has arrived) and a button (used to trigger the signal that the station's processing is complete).\nControl requirements:\n1. Mode Switching: The mode switch (Mode) is used to switch between manual and automatic modes of the production line.\n2. Manual Mode: In manual mode, the forward rotation button (ForwardButton) controls the forward rotation of the motor, and the reverse rotation button (ReverseButton) controls the reverse rotation of the motor. Forward and reverse rotation operations need to be interlocked and cannot be performed simultaneously.\n3. Automatic Mode:\n   - When the product arrives at Workstation A, SensorA detects the product, and after the operator triggers the processing complete signal via ButtonA, the motor starts forward rotation to move the product to Workstation B.\n   - When the product arrives at Workstation B, SensorB detects the product, the motor stops, and after the operator triggers the processing complete signal via ButtonB, the motor starts forward rotation to move the product to Workstation C.\n   - When the product arrives at Workstation C, SensorC detects the product, the motor stops, and after the operator triggers the processing complete signal via ButtonC, the completion indicator light (CompletionLight) turns on, indicating that the product processing is complete. When the product is taken away, i.e., SensorC no longer detects the product, the completion indicator light (CompletionLight) turns off.\n\n## Interface Definition\n\n| Direction | Variable/Field | Data Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Input | `Mode` | `BOOL` | Used to switch the production line between manual and automatic modes, 0=manual mode, 1=automatic mode |\n| Input | `ForwardButton` | `BOOL` | Forward rotation button |\n| Input | `ReverseButton` | `BOOL` | Reverse rotation button |\n| Input | `SensorA` | `BOOL` | Sensor A |\n| Input | `SensorB` | `BOOL` | Sensor B |\n| Input | `SensorC` | `BOOL` | Sensor C |\n| Input | `ButtonA` | `BOOL` | Button A |\n| Input | `ButtonB` | `BOOL` | Button B |\n| Input | `ButtonC` | `BOOL` | Button C |\n| Output | `MotorForward` | `BOOL` | Motor forward rotation output |\n| Output | `MotorReverse` | `BOOL` | Motor reverse rotation output |\n| Output | `CompletionLight` | `BOOL` | Indicator light for product processing completion |",
  "scenario": "A conveyor shares manual interlocking and an automatic three-station route.",
  "interface": [
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "Mode",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Used to switch the production line between manual and automatic modes, 0=manual mode, 1=automatic mode"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "ForwardButton",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Forward rotation button"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "ReverseButton",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Reverse rotation button"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "SensorA",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Sensor A"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "SensorB",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Sensor B"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "SensorC",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Sensor C"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "ButtonA",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Button A"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "ButtonB",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Button B"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "ButtonC",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Button C"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "MotorForward",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Motor forward rotation output"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "MotorReverse",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Motor reverse rotation output"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "CompletionLight",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Indicator light for product processing completion"
    }
  ],
  "initial_conditions": {
    "MotorForward": false,
    "MotorReverse": false,
    "CompletionLight": false,
    "phase": "WAIT_A"
  },
  "scan_semantics": "Inputs I[k] are sampled at invocation; outputs O[k] are observed after the call. Retained pre-state q[k] becomes q[k+1]. Each test resets the instance. A transition affects the same observed scan. dt_ms is elapsed time since the preceding invocation; the first invocation starts IEC timers at elapsed zero. CycleTime inputs, where supplied, are attributed to the current invocation rather than inferred from dt_ms.",
  "safety_priority": [
    "Forward and reverse are mutually exclusive.",
    "Destination arrival stops movement before processing resumes."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Opposing manual buttons produce neither direction.",
    "Buttons are level signals accepted only in their corresponding station wait. One phase transition is accepted per call.",
    "Entering manual mode clears automatic state and completion; return to automatic waits for A.",
    "Only one product is presented; station sensors are not contradictory.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values."
  ],
  "atomic_propositions": {
    "auto": "Mode",
    "fwd": "MotorForward after scan",
    "rev": "MotorReverse after scan",
    "mf": "ForwardButton AND NOT ReverseButton",
    "mr": "ReverseButton AND NOT ForwardButton",
    "arrive": "pre-phase MOVE_AB AND SensorB OR pre-phase MOVE_BC AND SensorC",
    "finish": "pre-phase WAIT_C AND SensorC AND ButtonC",
    "light": "CompletionLight",
    "removed": "NOT SensorC",
    "Mode": "I[k].Mode: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "ForwardButton": "I[k].ForwardButton: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "ReverseButton": "I[k].ReverseButton: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "SensorA": "I[k].SensorA: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "SensorB": "I[k].SensorB: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "SensorC": "I[k].SensorC: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "ButtonA": "I[k].ButtonA: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "ButtonB": "I[k].ButtonB: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "ButtonC": "I[k].ButtonC: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "MotorForward": "O[k].MotorForward: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "MotorReverse": "O[k].MotorReverse: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "CompletionLight": "O[k].CompletionLight: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "init": "At the separate pre-invocation initial observation before scan k=0: Spre.phase=\"WAIT_A\", O_init.MotorForward=false, O_init.MotorReverse=false, O_init.CompletionLight=false.",
    "phase_wait": "post-phase is WAIT_A, WAIT_B, or WAIT_C",
    "phase_move": "post-phase is MOVE_AB or MOVE_BC",
    "wait_phase": "post-phase is WAIT_A, WAIT_B, or WAIT_C",
    "move_phase": "post-phase is MOVE_AB or MOVE_BC",
    "done_phase": "post-phase is DONE"
  },
  "ltl": [
    {
      "id": "PUB011.P_init",
      "kind": "safety",
      "formula": "init",
      "description": "Before the first scan invocation, all declared OUTPUT variables and initial instance state hold their declared initial values.",
      "explanation": "Applies strictly to the fresh pre-invocation initial instance observation before scan k=0 (INITIAL_INSTANCE scope).",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "INITIAL_INSTANCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB011.P1",
      "name": "Interlock",
      "formula": "G(!(fwd & rev))",
      "explanation": "Motor directions are mutually exclusive.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB011.P2",
      "name": "Manual",
      "formula": "G(!auto -> ((fwd <-> mf) & (rev <-> mr)))",
      "explanation": "Manual level requests obey neutral conflict resolution.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB011.P3",
      "name": "Auto direction",
      "formula": "G(auto -> !rev)",
      "explanation": "Automatic routing only moves forward.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB011.P4",
      "name": "Arrival",
      "formula": "G(auto & arrive -> !fwd)",
      "explanation": "Arrival stops the motor in the observed scan.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB011.P5",
      "name": "Completion",
      "formula": "G(auto & finish -> light)",
      "explanation": "C completion asserts the light.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB011.P6",
      "name": "Removal",
      "formula": "G(auto & removed -> !light)",
      "explanation": "Removal clears completion.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB011.P7",
      "kind": "safety",
      "formula": "G(auto -> ((move_phase -> (fwd & !rev & !light)) & (wait_phase -> (!fwd & !rev & !light)) & (done_phase -> (!fwd & !rev & light))))",
      "description": "In automatic mode, WAIT_A/B/C keeps all outputs off, MOVE_AB/BC drives MotorForward only, and DONE lights CompletionLight only.",
      "explanation": "Prevents degenerate implementations that leave MotorForward FALSE in MOVE_* or mirror SensorC in DONE.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    }
  ]
}

ARCHITECTURAL PLAN:
{
  "state_machine": [
    {
      "name": "MANUAL",
      "outputs": "MotorForward = ForwardButton AND NOT ReverseButton; MotorReverse = ReverseButton AND NOT ForwardButton; CompletionLight = false; phase forced to WAIT_A",
      "transitions": [
        {
          "when": "Mode == true",
          "target": "WAIT_A",
          "action": "Return to automatic mode; wait for A; no automatic motion on entry"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "WAIT_A",
      "outputs": "MotorForward=false; MotorReverse=false; CompletionLight=false",
      "transitions": [
        {
          "when": "Mode == false",
          "target": "MANUAL",
          "action": "Clear automatic state and completion; stop automatic motion"
        },
        {
          "when": "Mode == true AND SensorA AND ButtonA",
          "target": "MOVE_AB",
          "action": "Start forward movement from A to B; one transition per scan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "MOVE_AB",
      "outputs": "MotorForward=true; MotorReverse=false; CompletionLight=false unless arrival transition applies in same scan",
      "transitions": [
        {
          "when": "Mode == false",
          "target": "MANUAL",
          "action": "Clear automatic state and completion; stop automatic motion"
        },
        {
          "when": "Mode == true AND SensorB",
          "target": "WAIT_B",
          "action": "Destination arrival stops forward output in same scan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "WAIT_B",
      "outputs": "MotorForward=false; MotorReverse=false; CompletionLight=false",
      "transitions": [
        {
          "when": "Mode == false",
          "target": "MANUAL",
          "action": "Clear automatic state and completion; stop automatic motion"
        },
        {
          "when": "Mode == true AND SensorB AND ButtonB",
          "target": "MOVE_BC",
          "action": "Start forward movement from B to C; one transition per scan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "MOVE_BC",
      "outputs": "MotorForward=true; MotorReverse=false; CompletionLight=false unless arrival transition applies in same scan",
      "transitions": [
        {
          "when": "Mode == false",
          "target": "MANUAL",
          "action": "Clear automatic state and completion; stop automatic motion"
        },
        {
          "when": "Mode == true AND SensorC",
          "target": "WAIT_C",
          "action": "Destination arrival stops forward output in same scan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "WAIT_C",
      "outputs": "MotorForward=false; MotorReverse=false; CompletionLight=false",
      "transitions": [
        {
          "when": "Mode == false",
          "target": "MANUAL",
          "action": "Clear automatic state and completion; stop automatic motion"
        },
        {
          "when": "Mode == true AND SensorC AND ButtonC",
          "target": "DONE",
          "action": "Assert CompletionLight in same scan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "DONE",
      "outputs": "MotorForward=false; MotorReverse=false; CompletionLight=true while SensorC remains true",
      "transitions": [
        {
          "when": "Mode == false",
          "target": "MANUAL",
          "action": "Clear automatic state and completion; stop automatic motion"
        },
        {
          "when": "Mode == true AND NOT SensorC",
          "target": "WAIT_A",
          "action": "Product removed; clear CompletionLight in same scan and wait for A"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "timer_plan": {
    "timers": [],
    "PT_durations": {},
    "reset_conditions": "None. No IEC timers are required by the specification; all transitions are level- and phase-qualified. If timers are added later, call their FBs unconditionally outside CASE/IF and reset them on Mode=FALSE, manual entry, or instance reset."
  },
  "priorities": [
    "Safety first: MotorForward and MotorReverse must never be true simultaneously.",
    "Manual conflict resolution: if ForwardButton and ReverseButton are both true, both motor direction outputs are false.",
    "Mode reset priority: entering manual mode clears automatic phase to WAIT_A and forces CompletionLight off.",
    "Destination arrival priority: SensorB in MOVE_AB or SensorC in MOVE_BC stops forward motion in the same scan before any next processing step.",
    "One automatic phase transition per scan; arrival stop has priority over station-complete start.",
    "Automatic mode allows forward motion only; reverse output is false in automatic mode.",
    "CompletionLight is on only in DONE while SensorC is true; removal of SensorC clears the light and returns to WAIT_A.",
    "Station buttons are accepted only when their corresponding sensor and wait phase are active.",
    "Outputs are assigned once in the final scan stage from the post-transition state, with a final mutual-exclusion interlock."
  ],
  "initial_values": {
    "phase": "WAIT_A",
    "state": "WAIT_A",
    "MotorForward": false,
    "MotorReverse": false,
    "CompletionLight": false,
    "ModePrev": false,
    "ForwardButtonPrev": false,
    "ReverseButtonPrev": false,
    "ButtonAPrev": false,
    "ButtonBPrev": false,
    "ButtonCPrev": false
  },
  "scan_execution_order": [
    {
      "stage": 1,
      "name": "edge sampling",
      "description": "Sample all inputs I[k] at invocation. Compute R_TRIG flags for Mode, ForwardButton, ReverseButton, ButtonA, ButtonB, and ButtonC for diagnostics and mode-entry detection. Automatic station acceptance uses level-qualified SensorX AND ButtonX per assumptions; edge flags do not create multiple transitions."
    },
    {
      "stage": 2,
      "name": "safety/reset priority and state transitions",
      "description": "Apply Mode=FALSE first: enter MANUAL, force phase=WAIT_A, clear automatic state and CompletionLight. Then apply automatic transitions in priority order: destination arrival stop (MOVE_AB AND SensorB -> WAIT_B; MOVE_BC AND SensorC -> WAIT_C), station complete start (WAIT_A AND SensorA AND ButtonA -> MOVE_AB; WAIT_B AND SensorB AND ButtonB -> MOVE_BC; WAIT_C AND SensorC AND ButtonC -> DONE), and removal (DONE AND NOT SensorC -> WAIT_A). At most one automatic phase transition per scan. Manual-to-auto entry goes to WAIT_A only."
    },
    {
      "stage": 3,
      "name": "unconditional top-level timer FB calls outside CASE/IF",
      "description": "No timer FBs are required. If timers are added for future debounce or delay, instantiate and call them unconditionally at top level outside CASE/IF; reset them on instance reset, Mode=FALSE, or manual entry."
    },
    {
      "stage": 4,
      "name": "unified output assignments",
      "description": "Assign MotorForward, MotorReverse, and CompletionLight exactly once from the post-transition state/phase. MANUAL: MotorForward=(ForwardButton AND NOT ReverseButton); MotorReverse=(ReverseButton AND NOT ForwardButton); CompletionLight=false. AUTO WAIT_A/WAIT_B/WAIT_C: all outputs false. AUTO MOVE_AB/MOVE_BC: MotorForward=true unless arrival transition moved to WAIT_B/WAIT_C in this scan; MotorReverse=false; CompletionLight=false. DONE: MotorForward=false; MotorReverse=false; CompletionLight=true while SensorC. Final interlock: if MotorForward AND MotorReverse then both are forced false."
    }
  ],
  "formal_assertions": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "formula": "G(!(MotorForward && MotorReverse))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "formula": "G((!Mode) -> ((MotorForward <-> (ForwardButton && !ReverseButton)) && (MotorReverse <-> (ReverseButton && !ForwardButton))))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "formula": "G(Mode -> !MotorReverse)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "formula": "G(CompletionLight -> SensorC)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "formula": "G((!Mode) -> !CompletionLight)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "formula": "G((Mode && SensorC) -> !MotorForward)"
    }
  ]
}

CODESYS DIALECT CARDS:
[
  {
    "id": "ton_timer",
    "title": "Standard IEC TON Timer Block Invocation",
    "body": "// Standard IEC TON timer: MUST invoke unconditionally OUTSIDE CASE/IF every scan!\nVAR\n    timer : TON;\n    runTimer : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\n// Control via boolean IN flag (never put timer(...) only inside an IF/CASE arm):\nrunTimer := (state = 1) AND NOT resetCmd;\ntimer(IN := runTimer, PT := T#2s);\nIF timer.Q THEN\n    // Timer expired; timer.ET holds elapsed time\nEND_IF;"
  },
  {
    "id": "case_state_machine",
    "title": "Explicit CASE State Machine Transitions",
    "body": "// 4-Stage Scan Order: 1) Edge sample 2) Reset/priority & CASE state transition\n// 3) Unconditional top-level TON/R_TRIG calls 4) Unified output assignments\nVAR\n    state : INT := 0; // 0=IDLE, 1=RUN, 2=FAULT\nEND_VAR\nIF emergencyStop THEN state := 2; END_IF;\nCASE state OF\n    0: IF startCmd AND NOT fault THEN state := 1; END_IF;\n    1: IF faultCmd THEN state := 2; ELSIF stopCmd THEN state := 0; END_IF;\n    2: IF resetCmd THEN state := 0; END_IF;\n    ELSE state := 0;\nEND_CASE;\noutActive := (state = 1); // Assign outputs unconditionally from current state"
  }
]

